> you think you can handle. Create a patch and send it in for review.

note that we're getting close to the next official release, which
means that any patches you submit that aren't absolutely critical for
proper kernel operation won't be applied.  it also means that there
are, most likely, a *truckload* of pending patches that will be
applied as soon as that release comes out.

so you might want to hold off until that release and the flurry of new
patches to get a good look at the up-to-date state of the source tree.
otherwise, you might start wasting time creating patches which are
already in the queue.

